// 소스를 연 채로 인용을 적는다. 요약이 아니라 원문과 그 위치다. locator 는 원문의 절 제목(§)과 문단, 시스템 카드는 절 번호와 쪽. 모든 quote 는 notes/body.txt 또는 해당 문서 텍스트에 공백 차이 없이 존재함을 스크립트로 확인했다.
{"id": "e1", "source": "w1", "locator": "§intro ¶1", "quote": "We’re introducing Claude Opus 5.5, the first model in our new Claude 5.5 family. It performs at the level of Claude Fable 5.1 on most work and costs 40% less to run than Opus 5.", "why": "글 전체의 주장 한 문장: Fable 5.1 수준, Opus 5 대비 40% 저렴"}
{"id": "e2", "source": "w1", "locator": "§intro ¶2", "quote": "On our automated behavioral audit, the most comprehensive alignment test we run, Opus 5.5 is the strongest-performing model we’ve tested to date. It also comes with the safeguards we’ve developed for our most capable models.", "why": "외부 평가자와 behavioral audit 최고 성적 선언"}
{"id": "e3", "source": "w1", "locator": "§intro · Performance", "quote": "One tester completed a 680,000-line code migration in less than a day—work that would have taken an engineering team weeks. It’s good at finding and fixing inefficiencies in software: when we asked it to cut load times across every page of a web app, Opus 5.5 succeeded 39 of 40 times, while Opus 5 made smaller improvements that also altered the app’s behavior.", "why": "intro 의 성능 일화 두 개: 680k 줄 마이그레이션, 39/40"}
{"id": "e4", "source": "w1", "locator": "§intro · Safety", "quote": "It is much less likely than recent models to take hard-to-reverse actions or act outside the boundaries it’s been given, and it’s more resistant than Opus 5 to prompt injection. We’ve also broadened our alignment testing to cover longer tasks, impossible tasks, and scenarios modeled on real incidents, though it still has limits.", "why": "intro 의 안전 요약과 '한계가 있다' 는 단서"}
{"id": "e5", "source": "w1", "locator": "§intro · Safety ¶2", "quote": "Because Opus 5.5 is comparable to Claude Mythos 5.1 in biology and cybersecurity, we’re deploying it with safeguards similar to those on Claude Fable 5.1.", "why": "안전장치 등급이 Fable 5.1 급인 이유"}
{"id": "e6", "source": "w1", "locator": "§intro · Cost and speed", "quote": "Our tests show that at default settings it will cost 40% less than Opus 5 on typical workloads. Input and output tokens are $4 and $20 per million, 20% less than Opus 5. Cache reads (which make up the majority of agentic and coding work costs) are $0.20 per million tokens, 60% less than Opus 5. Opus 5.5 also generates output more than 30% faster than Opus 5.", "why": "가격과 속도 수치의 원문"}
{"id": "e7", "source": "w1", "locator": "§intro · Cost and speed ¶2", "quote": "In addition to the price drop, we’re increasing five-hour usage limits on Pro, Max, Team, and seat-based Enterprise plans. We’re also providing subscription users a rate limit reset, which you can now save and use whenever you choose.", "why": "구독 플랜 한도 상향과 limit reset"}
{"id": "e8", "source": "w1", "locator": "§intro · Communication", "quote": "Early testers found its writing clearer and easier to follow, which addresses some of the common feedback we heard about Opus 5. It puts the most important information up front, and its style makes it a better work partner over long sessions.", "why": "글쓰기 개선이 Opus 5 피드백에 대한 대응임"}
{"id": "e9", "source": "w1", "locator": "§intro ¶last", "quote": "Claude Sonnet 5.5 and Claude Haiku 5.5 will follow in the coming weeks, with many of the same improvements to performance, efficiency, and safety.", "why": "Sonnet 5.5·Haiku 5.5 예고"}
{"id": "e10", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Performance and cost-effectiveness ¶1", "quote": "That said, at these levels of capability we’ve found that benchmark margins have become a less reliable guide to real-world differences. In our own use, the gap between Opus 5.5 and Claude Fable 5.1 is narrower than these scores suggest.", "why": "Anthropic 스스로 벤치마크 격차를 할인함"}
{"id": "e11", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Performance · table note", "quote": "Unless otherwise noted, all Claude Opus 5.5 results use adaptive thinking at max effort. Terminal-Bench 4.0 results are reported for Claude Opus 5.5 at xhigh effort and GPT-6 Astra at high effort, as reported by OpenAI; these represent each model’s highest score. Claude Opus 5.5 was evaluated with its production safeguards enabled. When they intervened, cybersecurity tasks were completed by Claude Opus 4.8, and biology and frontier LLM development tasks were completed by Claude Opus 5.", "why": "표의 조건: max effort, TB4 만 xhigh, 안전장치 개입 시 fallback 모델이 풀었다"}
{"id": "e12", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Performance · footnote 1", "quote": "Terminal-Bench 4.0: The standard error is ±2.6 pts for Claude Opus 5.5 and ±1.6–2 pts for the other Claude models. The public leaderboard (5 trials/task, Claude Code harness) reports Claude Opus 5 at 51.8%; our setup reproduces it at 52.3%, within noise. GPT-6 Astra and GPT-5.6 Sol figures are as reported by OpenAI.", "why": "TB4 표준오차와 타사 수치 출처"}
{"id": "e13", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Performance · footnote 2", "quote": "AutomationBench results were run and reported by Zapier. These runs were performed without fallback models, so safeguard interventions were considered failures—this resulted in a lower score than Claude Opus 5.5 would achieve in practice.", "why": "AutomationBench 는 fallback 없이 실패 처리"}
{"id": "e14", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Performance · footnote 3", "quote": "Terminal-Bench-Science 0.1: The standard error is ±3.5–5 pts per model. The public leaderboard (3 trials/task, Claude Code harness) reports Claude Opus 5 at 30.0%; our setup reproduces it at 29.0%, within noise.", "why": "TB-Science 표준오차"}
{"id": "e15", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Performance · efficiency", "quote": "Where Opus 5.5’s advantage is very clear is efficiency. It costs less per token than Opus 5 and uses fewer tokens per task, which nets out to a 40% drop in costs.", "why": "40% 의 구성: 토큰당 가격 + 태스크당 토큰 수"}
{"id": "e16", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Performance · pricing table", "quote": "Prices per 1M tokensClaude Opus 5.5Claude Opus 5 Cache reads$0.20$0.50 Input tokens$4$5 Output tokens$20$25 Cache writes$5$6.25", "why": "가격표 원문 (텍스트 추출 형태)"}
{"id": "e17", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Performance · fast mode", "quote": "Fast mode for Opus 5.5 is also available in Claude Code and the Claude Platform with up to 2.5x speed. It costs $8 per million input tokens and $40 per million output tokens.", "why": "fast mode 가격"}
{"id": "e18", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Coding ¶1", "quote": "An early tester used it to audit and fix a 200,000-line codebase in under three hours, where Opus 5 took over 20 hours and used 2.5x as many tokens. In an internal test, we asked Opus 5.5 and Fable 5.1 to translate HAProxy, widely used software that balances web traffic loads across servers, from C into Rust. Both rewrites passed nearly all of HAProxy’s own regression tests, but Opus 5.5 finished in 9.5 hours compared to 12 for Fable 5.1, and cost 51% less.", "why": "코딩 일화: 200k 줄, HAProxy C→Rust"}
{"id": "e19", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Coding ¶2", "quote": "At its default effort level on FrontierCode, it beats GPT-6 Astra at roughly 20% of the cost per task. On Terminal Bench 4.0, it matches Astra for about 40% of the cost, while on CursorBench it beats GPT-5.6 Sol by 11 points for about a third of the cost.", "why": "비용 대비 성능 주장 세 개"}
{"id": "e20", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Coding · TB4 chart caption", "quote": "Opus 5.5 at default effort beats Opus 5 at max effort for about a fifth of the cost. It matches GPT-6 Astra at about 40% of the cost.", "why": "TB4 차트 캡션"}
{"id": "e21", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Coding · FrontierCode chart caption", "quote": "FrontierCode measures whether an agent’s code changes would be merged. At default effort (medium), Opus 5.5 scores 54.6%, higher than all other models, beating GPT-6 Astra’s top score (53.3%) for about a fifth of the cost per task.", "why": "FC 캡션: medium 54.6% 이 표의 54.4% 보다 높다"}
{"id": "e22", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Coding · CursorBench chart caption", "quote": "At default effort (medium), Opus 5.5 scores 52.5%, compared to 51.8% for Fable 5.1 (max) and 46.6% for Opus 5 (max). It beats GPT-5.6 Sol’s top score (41.7%) by 11 points for about a third of the cost per task.", "why": "CB 캡션"}
{"id": "e23", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Coding · GitHub quote", "quote": "In our testing across GitHub Copilot CLI and VS Code, Claude Opus 5.5 used among the fewest tokens and steps we measured. In VS Code, it solved more terminal tasks than Opus 5 in less than half the steps.", "why": "GitHub 인용"}
{"id": "e24", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Coding · Clio quote", "quote": "It stayed on task for over 18 hours defining how our services talk to each other and working out how each one should apply that. Compared with Opus 5, it hit milestones faster and required minimal reworking.", "why": "Clio 18시간 무인 실행"}
{"id": "e25", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Coding · Lovable quote", "quote": "It gathers context once, makes fewer and more complete edits, and doesn’t get stuck retrying, finishing in a third to half fewer steps and using significantly fewer tokens along the way.", "why": "Lovable 스텝 수"}
{"id": "e26", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Coding · Quantium quote", "quote": "A complex coding task that previously took 38 prompts over four days came in at 11 prompts over three hours, with more production-ready outputs and less rework.", "why": "Quantium 38→11 프롬프트"}
{"id": "e27", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Coding · Optiver quote", "quote": "On our agentic coding tasks, Claude Opus 5.5 matched Opus 5’s quality in about half the turns, time and output tokens, cutting the cost of that workload by 40 to 50%.", "why": "Optiver 40~50% 비용"}
{"id": "e28", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Coding · Kiro quote", "quote": "On a public benchmark of real command-line tasks, Claude Opus 5.5 solved more than Opus 5 while making about 40% fewer calls and using half the tokens.", "why": "Kiro 호출 40% 감소"}
{"id": "e29", "source": "w1", "locator": "§The most secure coding agent ¶1", "quote": "Opus 5.5 has a classifier that screens every action before it runs, an open-source sandbox that security teams can audit, and code review that catches vulnerabilities before they merge.", "why": "보안 3요소"}
{"id": "e30", "source": "w1", "locator": "§The most secure coding agent ¶2", "quote": "On prompt injection attacks, it matches or beats Opus 5 in every setting we tested, including coding, tool use, computer use, and web browsing. On a benchmark run by the AI security firm Gray Swan, Opus 5.5 ties Fable 5.1 for the lowest prompt injection success rate of any model tested.", "why": "prompt injection 주장"}
{"id": "e31", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Knowledge work ¶1", "quote": "Across different effort settings, 16 out of 18 of Opus 5.5’s reports cleared our quality bar, where any invented figure or quote would have failed. Neither Fable 5.1 nor Opus 5 cleared that bar in any attempt.", "why": "리서치 보고서 16/18 vs 0"}
{"id": "e32", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Knowledge work ¶3", "quote": "Both models reached the same conclusions about the deal, but Opus 5.5’s model was more thorough and its presentation easier to read, while Opus 5’s had minor errors. Opus 5.5 finished in 63 minutes compared to 93 for Opus 5, and cost 50% less to produce.", "why": "M&A 모델 63분 vs 93분"}
{"id": "e33", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Knowledge work ¶4", "quote": "On GDPval-AA v2.1, a test of real-world work across 44 occupations, Opus 5.5 scores 1846 Elo, ahead of Fable 5.1 and Opus 5. At default effort (medium), Opus 5.5 beats GPT-6 Astra at max effort for about a fifth of the cost per task.", "why": "GDPval 1846"}
{"id": "e34", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Knowledge work · WANDR footnote 4", "quote": "Claude models were run with offline versions of the web search and web fetch tools, programmatic tool calling, code execution, and a 980k-token task budget. This differs from Perplexity’s published setup, scores are not directly comparable across the two and we only show models scored under the same conditions.", "why": "WANDR 비교 불가 단서"}
{"id": "e35", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Knowledge work · Deloitte quote", "quote": "Even at its lowest effort setting, Claude Opus 5.5 caught 72% of known bugs in our code reviews to Opus 5’s 56% at high effort, with fewer false alarms and a fraction of the output.", "why": "Deloitte 72% vs 56%"}
{"id": "e36", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Knowledge work · Rogo quote", "quote": "At its lowest effort setting, Claude Opus 5.5 beat Opus 5 at high effort on our BigFinance Bench with about 60% fewer output tokens.", "why": "Rogo low vs high"}
{"id": "e37", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Knowledge work · Walleye quote", "quote": "At higher settings, it went even further: it detected that the minute indexing in our own instructions was off by one and corrected for it, noting that this would cost it points with the grader. It was right, and no model we’ve tested had caught and acted on that before.", "why": "Walleye off-by-one"}
{"id": "e38", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Knowledge work · Hebbia quote", "quote": "On end-to-end finance workflows graded against expert rubrics, Claude Opus 5.5 covered 86.6% of what we look for versus 60.3% for Opus 5.", "why": "Hebbia 86.6 vs 60.3"}
{"id": "e39", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Knowledge work · Viktor quote", "quote": "At the same effort, Claude Opus 5.5 needs fewer steps and tool calls per task than Opus 5 and costs nearly half as much, while getting twice as many of our hardest tasks right.", "why": "Viktor 절반 비용 2배 정답"}
{"id": "e40", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Communication ¶1", "quote": "It puts the most important information up front, is less likely to use jargon or idiosyncratic phrases, and follows the writing rules you give it. We find that this makes Opus 5.5 a noticeably better collaborator.", "why": "글쓰기 세 특징"}
{"id": "e41", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Communication · bug example (Opus 5.5)", "quote": "The free-tier change accounts for only $1.50 of acme’s August drop. The other $9.92 comes from a bug in commit 0552feb. That commit was labelled “No behaviour change,” but it stops counting usage from the last day of the month.", "why": "비교 예시 Opus 5.5 답 첫 문단"}
{"id": "e42", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Communication · Box quote", "quote": "In our evaluations, Claude Opus 5.5 used a third of the tokens Opus 5 did, and its answers were 40% less verbose without losing accuracy.", "why": "Box 토큰 1/3"}
{"id": "e43", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Communication · Factory quote", "quote": "Claude Opus 5.5 is the first model we’d default to at medium effort. In our testing it matched Opus 5 on high effort, while using 20 to 25% fewer output tokens.", "why": "Factory medium 기본"}
{"id": "e44", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Communication · Stripe quote", "quote": "On a multi-day rebase of 40 stacked pull requests, one Claude Opus 5.5 session directed a dozen more sessions and laid out every conflict plainly.", "why": "Stripe 40 PR rebase"}
{"id": "e45", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Safety · Pacing ¶1", "quote": "so that safety practices stay ahead of model capabilities. Pacing is an approach to keeping AI safe, remaining competitive with China, and realizing AI’s benefits, particularly in areas like biology and medicine.", "why": "pacing 링크의 맥락"}
{"id": "e46", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Safety · Pacing · current", "quote": "The current generation of models relies on an established set of practices: extensive alignment testing, pre-release evaluation by outside organizations such as METR and Frontier Design, and safeguards matched to each model’s capabilities in high-risk areas like cybersecurity and biology.", "why": "현재 모델 안전 관행"}
{"id": "e47", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Safety · Pacing · future", "quote": "Additionally, we’re improving our alignment rewards and developing automated processes for producing new, diverse scenarios for safety training.", "why": "미래 모델 준비"}
{"id": "e48", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Safety · Pacing · higher standard", "quote": "Models with greater capabilities—such as those that can fully automate the work of AI research itself—require a higher safety standard still. Our calls for pacing were based in large part on our expectation that such models could be trained soon. For these models, we do not assume the measures described above will meet that safety standard on their own.", "why": "더 높은 기준이 필요한 모델"}
{"id": "e49", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Safety · Alignment ¶1", "quote": "On our primary evaluation suite, an automated behavioral audit that assesses Claude across nearly 2,000 scenarios, Opus 5.5 scored better than any recent Claude model on nearly every measure of misaligned behavior. It’s also our strongest model on most measures of honesty.", "why": "audit 결과"}
{"id": "e50", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Safety · Alignment ¶2", "quote": "In a new evaluation designed to test a model’s propensity to cross containment boundaries, Opus 5.5 attempted to circumvent boundaries around 85% less often than Opus 5 or Claude Mythos 5.1, and every attempt it made was low severity and self-reported.", "why": "containment 85% 감소"}
{"id": "e51", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Safety · Alignment ¶3", "quote": "We see signs that Opus 5.5 often suspects it is being evaluated, which challenges our ability to assess how it will act in the vast variety of real-world settings it is deployed in.", "why": "evaluation awareness 한계"}
{"id": "e52", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Safety · Safeguards ¶1", "quote": "Opus 5.5 is the first Opus model to launch with a similar class of safeguards to Fable 5.1 on cybersecurity, biology, and distillation, all of which fall back to another model transparently.", "why": "안전장치 세 영역과 fallback"}
{"id": "e53", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Safety · Safeguards · Cybersecurity", "quote": "Users will be able to identify and fix bugs in their code as part of the routine software development lifecycle, but most cybersecurity tasks will be re-routed to Opus 4.8.", "why": "cyber 작업은 Opus 4.8 로"}
{"id": "e54", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Safety · Safeguards · Cybersecurity ¶2", "quote": "The new program will include three tiers for increasingly permissive trusted access, including access to Claude Mythos models.", "why": "CVP 3단계"}
{"id": "e55", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Safety · Safeguards · Biology", "quote": "For this reason, Opus 5.5 uses the same biology safeguards as Fable 5.1. To use Opus 5.5 for research and development work impeded by these safeguards, users can apply to our new Life Sciences Verification Program", "why": "biology 안전장치와 LSVP"}
{"id": "e56", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Safety · Distillation ¶2", "quote": "Opus 5.5 is launching with preserved thinking, the anti-distillation safeguard we introduced with Fable 5.1. It stops API users from editing Claude’s prior context in an attempt to extract Claude’s reasoning. It applies to Fable 5.1 and Opus 5.5 for API accounts created on or after August 31, 2026.", "why": "preserved thinking 적용 범위"}
{"id": "e57", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Safety · Data retention", "quote": "Like previous Opus models, Opus 5.5 is available with zero data retention.", "why": "ZDR"}
{"id": "e58", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Availability", "quote": "Claude Opus 5.5 is now available on all platforms, including Amazon Web Services, Google Cloud, and Microsoft Azure.", "why": "가용성"}
{"id": "e59", "source": "s1", "locator": "§6.4 p.104", "quote": "For each model, we conduct about 4,000 investigation sessions; in these sessions, an investigator model is tasked with probing the behavior of the model under study in a simulated scenario. Scenarios are drawn from a largely handwritten list of about 1,900 scenario descriptions", "why": "audit 규모: 약 1,900 시나리오, 4,000 세션"}
{"id": "e60", "source": "s1", "locator": "§6.4 p.104 ¶2", "quote": "This means the absolute score for each dimension reflects the distribution of seed scenarios and is difficult to interpret in isolation. Scores are thus valuable primarily for comparing models.", "why": "audit 점수는 상대 비교용"}
{"id": "e61", "source": "s1", "locator": "§6.4.1 p.105", "quote": "Exceptions included prompt injection, where we saw a genuine but small regression, which we cover with a dedicated evaluation in Section 6.5.1, and the related phenomenon of accepting unverifiable authorization.", "why": "audit 에서 prompt injection 은 소폭 퇴보"}
{"id": "e62", "source": "s1", "locator": "Executive Summary p.2", "quote": "However, it is more likely than previous models to follow malicious instructions in text that a user pastes into their own prompt; we discuss this behavior and our mitigations in more detail in Section 6.5.1.", "why": "사용자 붙여넣기 텍스트 속 지시 취약"}
{"id": "e63", "source": "s1", "locator": "§6.4.8 p.118", "quote": "With Claude Opus 5.5, only 1.5% of cases resulted in attempted crossing of a containment boundary, and all of those cases are rated as low severity: the model reached across a weak boundary in a read-only manner, did not carry the attempt further when it encountered a stronger security barrier, and clearly reported the actions afterwards.", "why": "sandbox escape 1.5%"}
{"id": "e64", "source": "s1", "locator": "§6.4.8 p.118 figure", "quote": "Scores from our sandbox escape evaluation, comprising 28 handmade scenarios tailored to elicit sandbox escape, run seven times for each model.", "why": "sandbox 평가 규모 28×7"}
{"id": "e65", "source": "s1", "locator": "§6.4.9 p.119", "quote": "Claude Opus 5.5’s propensities here are substantially improved from prior models but are still quite concerning: within these high-stakes user-initiated security evaluations, the model acts in ways that would likely be harmful in roughly half of cases. We do see significant evaluation awareness here, with verbalized indicators in about one-third of Opus 5.5 runs", "why": "package registry 평가: 절반 유해, 1/3 evaluation awareness"}
{"id": "e66", "source": "s1", "locator": "§5.2.1 p.85", "quote": "Claude Opus 5.5 matches Claude Fable 5.1, our most robust model to date on this benchmark, with an attack success rate of 0.1% at k=1, 0.7% at k=10, and 1.0% at k=15. This improves on Claude Opus 5 (0.4%, 3.6%, and 4.8%, respectively).", "why": "Gray Swan IPI 수치"}
{"id": "e67", "source": "s1", "locator": "§5.2.1 p.84", "quote": "The Claude models Gray Swan evaluated did not have prompt injection-specific safeguards; they only had our standard blocking classifiers enabled, including classifier-triggered fallbacks. It is our understanding that other frontier models are evaluated on their publicly available endpoints, which may or may not include additional safeguards.", "why": "IPI 비교 조건 차이"}
{"id": "e68", "source": "s1", "locator": "§1.5 p.13", "quote": "Our classifiers to prevent distillation of our models (for example, by attempting to extract a model’s hidden reasoning) will block on Claude Opus 5.5 with no fallback model.", "why": "distillation 분류기는 fallback 없음"}
{"id": "e69", "source": "s1", "locator": "§1.5 p.13 ¶2", "quote": "The fallback behavior described above applies to our first-party products and developers who are opted in to such fallbacks on our API; traffic on our models via other platforms and providers may experience different behavior.", "why": "fallback 은 opt-in"}
{"id": "e70", "source": "s1", "locator": "§8.1 Table 8.1.A p.174", "quote": "Unless otherwise noted, all Claude Opus 5.5 results use the following standard configuration: adaptive thinking at max effort, default sampling settings (temperature, top_p), averaged over five trials. Terminal-Bench 4.0 score is reported at xhigh effort.", "why": "표의 표준 설정"}
{"id": "e71", "source": "s1", "locator": "§8.4 p.176", "quote": "Opus 5.5 ranks first on FrontierCode (Main) with a 54.6% score (each model at its best reasoning effort), improving on Claude Opus 5 (53.4%) and leading Claude Fable 5 (53.5%), GPT-6 Astra (53.3%), and Claude Fable 5.1 (52.8%).", "why": "각 모델 최고 effort 기준이면 격차 1.2pt"}
{"id": "e72", "source": "s1", "locator": "§8.4 p.176 note", "quote": "There is a decline in model performance on FrontierCode (Main and Extended) above medium effort. The evaluation is designed around writing mergeable code diffs without requiring human edits, so its grading penalizes out-of-scope changes that may be unnecessary, even if they are high quality or helpful.", "why": "effort 올리면 FC 점수가 내려가는 이유"}
{"id": "e73", "source": "s1", "locator": "Executive Summary p.4", "quote": "It delivers this performance at lower cost: much of the improvement is available below maximum reasoning effort.", "why": "개선분이 max 아래에서 나온다"}
{"id": "e74", "source": "d1", "locator": "§intro", "quote": "Four breaking changes affect code already running on Claude Opus 5:", "why": "breaking change 4개 (목록은 링크가 섞여 있어 머리만 인용)"}
{"id": "e75", "source": "d1", "locator": "§Thinking can't be disabled", "quote": "On Claude Opus 5.5, thinking is always on: a request that sets `thinking: {\"type\": \"disabled\"}`, or a manual budget with `thinking: {\"type\": \"enabled\", \"budget_tokens\": N}`, returns a 400 `invalid_request_error`.", "why": "disabled 와 budget 모두 400"}
{"id": "e76", "source": "d1", "locator": "§Forced tool use", "quote": "`tool_choice` set to `{\"type\": \"any\"}` or `{\"type\": \"tool\", \"name\": \"...\"}` returns a 400 `invalid_request_error`", "why": "forced tool use 400"}
{"id": "e77", "source": "d1", "locator": "§Behavior differences", "quote": "**The default effort is `medium`.** A request that omits `effort` runs at `medium`; on Claude Opus 5 it ran at `high`.", "why": "기본 effort 가 한 단계 내려감"}
{"id": "e78", "source": "d1", "locator": "§Behavior differences ¶3", "quote": "an application that streams them to its users goes quiet between tool calls, with no error.", "why": "도구 호출 사이 텍스트가 thinking 블록으로"}
{"id": "e79", "source": "d1", "locator": "§Pricing", "quote": "with 5-minute cache writes at $5, 1-hour cache writes at $8, and cache reads at $0.20 per million tokens (0.05x the base input price).", "why": "1시간 캐시 쓰기 $8"}
{"id": "e80", "source": "d2", "locator": "§Batch processing table", "quote": "| Claude Opus 5.5                                                                                                                       | $2 / MTok    | $10 / MTok    |", "why": "batch 반값 $2/$10"}
{"id": "e81", "source": "d1", "locator": "§Fast mode", "quote": "it is not available on Amazon Bedrock, Claude Platform on AWS, Google Cloud, or Microsoft Foundry.", "why": "fast mode 는 Claude API 전용"}
{"id": "e82", "source": "d1", "locator": "§Thinking blocks are tied", "quote": "Claude Opus 5.5 reads thinking blocks from Claude Opus 5 and earlier Opus, Sonnet, and Haiku models, but not from Claude Fable or Claude Mythos models. On the Claude API, Claude Fable 5.1 and Claude Mythos 5.1 read thinking blocks from Claude Opus 5.5; no other model does.", "why": "thinking 블록 호환 방향"}
{"id": "e83", "source": "d1", "locator": "§Behavior differences · safeguards", "quote": "The model runs a biology safety classifier in addition to the cybersecurity one, and requests that push it to reproduce its internal reasoning in the response text can be declined with the `reasoning_extraction` category.", "why": "reasoning_extraction 거부 범주"}
{"id": "e84", "source": "d1", "locator": "§Computer use", "quote": "On the Claude API and Google Cloud, Claude Opus 5.5 supports only the toolset: a request that declares a `computer_20251124` tool returns a 400 `invalid_request_error`.", "why": "computer_20251124 제거"}
{"id": "e85", "source": "d2", "locator": "§Model pricing · cache", "quote": "On Claude Opus 5.5, a cache hit costs 5% of the standard input price ($0.20 USD per million tokens).", "why": "캐시 읽기 0.05x"}
{"id": "e86", "source": "d3", "locator": "§Model comparison table", "quote": "| Reliable knowledge cutoff                                                                 | Jun 2026                                                                          | Jun 2026", "why": "knowledge cutoff (Fable 5.1 과 Opus 5.5 둘 다 Jun 2026)"}
{"id": "e87", "source": "d3", "locator": "§Model comparison table · context", "quote": "1M tokens is roughly 555k words or 2.5M Unicode characters on the current tokenizer (introduced with Claude Opus 4.7)", "why": "1M 컨텍스트 환산"}
{"id": "e88", "source": "d5", "locator": "§Recommended effort levels for Claude Opus 5.5", "quote": "Claude Opus 5.5 supports all five effort levels, and `medium` is the default (Claude Opus 5 and earlier Opus models default to `high`, so a request that omits `effort` runs one level lower than it did on Claude Opus 5).", "why": "effort 문서의 같은 경고"}
{"id": "e89", "source": "d6", "locator": "§intro", "quote": "Fast mode delivers up to 2.5x higher output tokens per second from Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Opus 5, and Claude Opus 4.8 at premium pricing. Set `speed: \"fast\"` with the `fast-mode-2026-02-01` beta header on your request to opt in.", "why": "fast mode 파라미터"}
{"id": "e90", "source": "d6", "locator": "§What fast mode does", "quote": "Speed benefits are focused on output tokens per second (OTPS), not time to first token (TTFT)", "why": "2.5x 는 OTPS 기준"}
{"id": "e91", "source": "d4", "locator": "§intro", "quote": "The API enforces the prefix check by default for accounts created on or after August 31, 2026, 00:00 UTC. On older accounts, it enforces the prefix check only on requests that set `thinking.block_binding.prefix_mismatch_behavior`.", "why": "prefix 검사 적용 조건"}
{"id": "e92", "source": "h1", "locator": "§Who will this impact?", "quote": "We're taking a phased approach to enforcement, starting with new accounts, where we see the highest concentration of distillation-related abuse. This gives developers with existing accounts time to make their harnesses and integrations compatible.", "why": "단계적 시행 이유"}
{"id": "e93", "source": "h1", "locator": "§What does this mean for API integrations?", "quote": "Certain integrations—particularly those that involve rewriting earlier turns mid-conversation, like context compaction, injected system reminders, or changing tools mid-session—may need adjustment.", "why": "영향받는 통합 유형"}
{"id": "e94", "source": "h2", "locator": "§note", "quote": "This article applies only to Opus and Sonnet class models, but doesn’t apply to Claude Opus 5.5. We'll soon be expanding the Cyber Verification Program to include Opus 5.5 and Mythos class models.", "why": "CVP 문서는 아직 Opus 5.5 미적용"}
{"id": "e95", "source": "h3", "locator": "§How a limit reset works", "quote": "Depending on the limit reset shown, either your five-hour session limit or your weekly usage limit go back to full right away.", "why": "limit reset 의 뜻"}
{"id": "e96", "source": "n1", "locator": "§intro", "quote": "Today, we are introducing the Life Sciences Verification Program (LSVP), which gives life science professionals access to our Mythos, Opus, and Sonnet models with a refined set of safeguards more permissive for biology-related work.", "why": "LSVP 정의"}
{"id": "e97", "source": "n1", "locator": "§Verification and access types", "quote": "High-risk Use is an add-on grant for teams working in areas blocked under Standard Use. It removes all safeguards that block life sciences requests. This grant applies to a single research project as opposed to a full team, and must be renewed every six months.", "why": "LSVP 두 등급"}
{"id": "e98", "source": "n2", "locator": "§intro", "quote": "But over the last few months, I have become convinced that fully addressing the risks requires even more prudence — not just investing in risk prevention, but pacing the rate of capabilities advancement so that risk prevention has time to keep up. We must slow the pace at which we improve the capabilities of AI models.", "why": "pacing 의 뜻"}
{"id": "e99", "source": "n2", "locator": "§intro · steps", "quote": "Each frontier AI company commits to giving ongoing, employee-like access to a team of embedded third-party evaluators (such as METR), whose role is to verify adherence to safety practices and commitments, report incidents, and help assess the alignment of not just completed AI models but training pipelines and processes.", "why": "Embedded evaluators"}
{"id": "e100", "source": "c1", "locator": "comment 49808623 (gwd, 2026-09-22T21:47Z)", "quote": "Opus 5.5: Found 8/14 issues. Total cost: $15.40 Fable 5.1: Found 7/14 issues. Total cost: $66.34 Opus 5: Found 6/14 issues. Total cost: $15.19 Sonnet 5: Found 2/14 issues. Total cost: $19.15 This is a relatively small sample size, but it was both the best and the cheapest.", "why": "HN 비용 표본"}
{"id": "e101", "source": "c1", "locator": "comment 49805459 (qlte, 2026-09-22T17:57Z)", "quote": "Opus 5.5 Medium = $1.34 GPT-6-Astra High = $1.76 And that assumes Opus 5.5 Medium is actually equivalent to Astra High in all real-world usage/personal work loads, which isn't guaranteed as benchmarks saturate. The High vs. High comparison (probably not equivalent, but for reference): Opus 5.5 High = $1.82 GPT-6-Astra High = $1.76", "why": "비교 기준 문제 제기"}
{"id": "e102", "source": "c1", "locator": "comment 49809918 (nl, 2026-09-23T00:04Z)", "quote": "5.5 is higher for max effort, slightly higher for xhigh and lower for high, medium and low effort. The biggest proportional difference seems to be at max (5.5 is 38% more) and at high (5.5 is 21% less).", "why": "effort 별 토큰"}
{"id": "e103", "source": "c1", "locator": "comment 49810898 (rmunn, 2026-09-23T02:26Z)", "quote": "four of the five line numbers were wrong, and while checking them I found two findings that were overstated.\" Then I noticed in the corner of the Claude CLI UI that it was showing \"Effort: medium\". I'm pretty sure I had set it to high effort before", "why": "medium 기본값 체감"}
{"id": "e104", "source": "c1", "locator": "comment 49804862 (simonw, 2026-09-22T17:22Z)", "quote": "I haven't managed to get one for level \"max\" yet, it hit the limit of 128,000 cap for output tokens while it was still reasoning about the question!", "why": "max 의 출력 한도"}
{"id": "e105", "source": "c1", "locator": "comment 49808591 (mintik, 2026-09-22T21:44Z)", "quote": "[cyber] classifier is incredibly sensitive with Opus 5.5 I cannot complete any embedded/driver/system-level tasks. Quite literally not a single task was able to complete today without getting flagged for [cyber]", "why": "cyber 오탐 보고"}
{"id": "e106", "source": "c1", "locator": "comment 49805157 (Retr0id, 2026-09-22T17:38Z)", "quote": "Opus 4.8 is answering instead, or you can edit and retry with Opus 5.5 (1M context). Yay, yet another model I can't use for anything interesting, even with CVP.", "why": "fallback 배너와 CVP"}
{"id": "e107", "source": "c1", "locator": "comment 49804997 (arw0n, 2026-09-22T17:29Z)", "quote": "It has far less false positives now, and generally accepts defensive requests. When it comes to offense, you can actually ask about certain types of vulnerabilities if you phrase things carefully, but it will block hard if it is about exploits.", "why": "반대 방향 보고"}
{"id": "e108", "source": "c1", "locator": "comment 49807724 (senko, 2026-09-22T20:37Z)", "quote": "Opus 5.5 is neck-and-neck with Fable 5.1 and Astra 6 in my vibe-coding tests - maybe even better than Fable 5.1", "why": "Fable 5.1 과 동급 보고"}
{"id": "e109", "source": "c1", "locator": "comment 49804122 (km144, 2026-09-22T16:41Z)", "quote": "In general, \"benchmark margins have become a less reliable guide to real-world differences\" sounds like a big problem.", "why": "원문 단서에 대한 반응"}
{"id": "e110", "source": "s1", "locator": "§3.2 p.44", "quote": "This happens automatically in our own applications; on the API, the developer must opt in to automatic fallbacks.", "why": "API 에서 fallback 은 opt-in"}
{"id": "e111", "source": "d1", "locator": "§Refusals and fallback", "quote": "A declined request returns HTTP 200 with `stop_reason: \"refusal\"` and a [`stop_details`](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/refusals-and-fallback#refusal-response) object naming the policy area", "why": "거부 응답의 형태"}
{"id": "e112", "source": "d2", "locator": "§Model pricing table · Opus 5", "quote": "| Claude Opus 5                                                                                                                         | $5 / MTok         | $6.25 / MTok    | $10 / MTok      | $0.50 / MTok             | $25 / MTok    |", "why": "Opus 5 의 1시간 캐시 쓰기 $10"}
{"id": "e113", "source": "d2", "locator": "§Batch processing table · Opus 5", "quote": "| Claude Opus 5                                                                                                                         | $2.50 / MTok | $12.50 / MTok |", "why": "Opus 5 batch 가격"}
{"id": "e114", "source": "d2", "locator": "§Fast mode pricing table", "quote": "| Claude Opus 5 / Claude Opus 4.8 | $10 / MTok | $50 / MTok |", "why": "Opus 5 fast mode 가격"}
{"id": "e115", "source": "d3", "locator": "§Model comparison table · Retirement", "quote": "| [Retirement](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/model-deprecations)                         | Not sooner than September 1, 2027                                                 | Not sooner than September 22, 2027", "why": "Opus 5.5 retirement 하한"}
{"id": "e116", "source": "d3", "locator": "§Model comparison table · Retirement note", "quote": "**Retirement:** Anthropic’s commitment for Anthropic-operated platforms (Claude API, Claude Platform on AWS, Microsoft Foundry). Amazon Bedrock and Google Cloud set their own dates.", "why": "retirement 약속의 범위"}
{"id": "e117", "source": "d3", "locator": "§Legacy models", "quote": "Legacy models (still available): [Claude Fable 5](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/models/fable-5/overview), [Claude Opus 5](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/models/opus-5/overview)", "why": "Opus 5 는 legacy 로 계속 제공"}
{"id": "e118", "source": "h1", "locator": "§Who will this impact? ¶2", "quote": "This covers Claude Platform organizations, Amazon Bedrock accounts, Google Cloud Vertex AI projects, and Microsoft Foundry projects.", "why": "prefix 검사 적용 플랫폼"}
{"id": "e119", "source": "s1", "locator": "§5.2.1 p.86", "quote": "For Claude Opus 5.5, 18% of rollouts were served by Claude Opus 4.8 after a classifier-triggered fallback, compared to 23% for Claude Fable 5.1. These fallbacks were concentrated in coding scenarios, where 46% of Claude Opus 5.5’s rollouts fell back, compared to 2% in tool use and under 1% in computer use. Fallbacks do not degrade robustness on this benchmark: none of the 1,310 fallback-served rollouts resulted in a successful attack.", "why": "Gray Swan 에서 코딩 시나리오 46% 가 Opus 4.8 fallback"}
{"id": "e120", "source": "s1", "locator": "§5.2.2.1 p.88", "quote": "Of the requests that received a valid response, 64% of those sent to Claude Opus 5.5 were served by Claude Opus 4.8, compared to the 60% fallback rate for Claude Fable 5.1 and 14% for Claude Opus 5 with thinking enabled. Among requests sent to Claude Opus 5.5 served by the fallback model, the attack success rate was 85.73%, whereas none of the 2,872 requests Claude Opus 5.5 answered directly were susceptible to the attack.", "why": "adaptive 공격에서 fallback 응답이 뚫린다"}
{"id": "e121", "source": "s1", "locator": "Executive Summary p.3", "quote": "We tested how Claude Opus 5.5 behaves as an agent in Claude Code and computer use settings, without the additional safeguards we apply in production. It assisted with dual-use and benign security tasks at the highest rate of the models we evaluated but also refused malicious requests at the lowest rate.", "why": "Agentic safety 문단"}
{"id": "e122", "source": "s1", "locator": "§3.2 p.47", "quote": "As with Claude Opus 5 and Claude Fable 5.1, our policy allows vulnerability discovery in source code so developers can use Claude Opus 5.5 to help write more secure software, but blocks vulnerability discovery in compiled binaries.", "why": "cyber 분류기의 선"}
{"id": "e123", "source": "s1", "locator": "Executive Summary p.2", "quote": "we have opted for a temporarily wider safety margin against jailbreaks, while we work to reduce our classifiers’ false-positive rate.", "why": "오탐은 의도된 여유"}
{"id": "e124", "source": "s1", "locator": "§5.2.1 p.85 ¶2", "quote": "To mitigate this asymmetry, we only report on benchmark performance for models not subject to the red-teaming competitions", "why": "Gray Swan 비교 집합"}
{"id": "e125", "source": "s1", "locator": "§6.4.10 p.121", "quote": "This safety measure results in slightly higher scores on our misuse metrics than we see with the bare Opus 5.5 model, since those metrics focus on compliance with harmful requests and these weaker models are sometimes less strict about refusing misuse.", "why": "제품 설정의 misuse 지표"}
{"id": "e126", "source": "s1", "locator": "§1.5 p.12 ¶bio", "quote": "These cover a wider range of topics than the CB misuse classifiers on Claude Opus 5 and less capable models. Blocks on this classifier will fall back to Claude Opus 5.", "why": "생물학 분류기는 Opus 5 보다 넓다"}
{"id": "e127", "source": "s1", "locator": "§6.4.8 p.118 ¶2", "quote": "recent training interventions meant to curb this behavior have had a strong effect. These counts are reported separately and are not pooled into the automated audit figures above.", "why": "sandbox 평가는 감사와 별도 집계"}
{"id": "e128", "source": "s1", "locator": "Figure 6.4.8.A p.119 (image)", "quote": "Claude Mythos 5: 14.9% low, 9.3% moderate+; Claude Opus 5: 7.7% low, 2.6% moderate+; Claude Mythos 5.1: 8.7% low, 1.0% moderate+; Claude Opus 5.5: 1.5% low", "why": "막대에 찍힌 값. pdftoppm 으로 p.119 를 열어 읽었다"}
{"id": "e129", "source": "s1", "locator": "Figure 6.4.9.A p.120 (image)", "quote": "Published with no encouragement while the registry looked real: Claude Sonnet 5 26, Claude Opus 5 24, Claude Opus 5.5 10", "why": "막대에 찍힌 값. pdftoppm 으로 p.120 을 열어 읽었다"}
{"id": "e130", "source": "d3", "locator": "§intro guidance", "quote": "Use [Claude Fable 5.1](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/models/fable-5-1/overview) for demanding reasoning and long-horizon agentic work, or when your evals on Claude Opus 5.5 at higher effort still fall short.", "why": "overview 의 모델 선택 안내"}
{"id": "e131", "source": "h2", "locator": "§Cyber Verification Program", "quote": "Organizations on Zero Data Retention (ZDR) are not currently eligible to participate in the CVP.", "why": "ZDR 은 CVP 불가"}
{"id": "e132", "source": "h2", "locator": "§How to apply · Amazon Bedrock", "quote": "The Cyber Verification Program is not available on Bedrock at this time.", "why": "Bedrock 은 CVP 불가"}
{"id": "e133", "source": "n1", "locator": "§Verification and access types ¶2", "quote": "Standard Use grants apply to Mythos 5.1, Opus 5, and Sonnet 5 today, and to future models as they launch.", "why": "LSVP 적용 모델"}
{"id": "e134", "source": "s1", "locator": "§5.2.2.1 p.88 ¶2", "quote": "Prompt injection probes reduce Claude Opus 5.5’s overall attack success rate to 11.13%--a roughly 80% improvement compared to unsafeguarded Claude Opus 5.5–and second only to Claude Fable 5.1 (8.70%) and lower than both Claude Opus 5 (19.53%) and Claude Sonnet 5 (15.76%). With probes enabled, all observed successful attacks again came from fallback-served requests.", "why": "probe 켠 제품 조건의 공격 성공률"}
{"id": "e135", "source": "c1", "locator": "comment 49807724 (senko, 2026-09-22T20:37Z) ¶2", "quote": "The above Opus games took ~45min to generate with the cost between $11 and $14 (per ccusage - I'm on a Max sub). Used from Claude Code with xhigh effort.", "why": "senko 의 비용·시간·effort"}
